# KeyMatrix (T8 Toggle inventory, docs/ui-plan.md "KeyMatrix"): every [keys] row is pressed once on dolpic/0 (down, 30 frames,
# up); the PAD trace shows which bits or axes change. One route serves all runs, the INI decides what a key does:
#   Lauf A (km_a, no [keys] section): the standard keys (src/sdk/pad_keys.cpp defaults) set their bits; the second set does nothing.
#   Lauf B (km_b, [keys] with the second set): the second set sets the bits; the standard keys do nothing.
#     INI rows: A=23, B=10, X=6, Y=25, START=30, Z=17, L=16, R=11, DPAD_UP=31, DPAD_DOWN=32, DPAD_LEFT=33, DPAD_RIGHT=34, STICK_UP=18, STICK_DOWN=19, STICK_LEFT=24, STICK_RIGHT=21, CSTICK_UP=5, CSTICK_DOWN=27, CSTICK_LEFT=28, CSTICK_RIGHT=35
# Order: standard 19, second 19, Return (standard START), 1 (START of Lauf B). START pauses the game, so it comes last.
# Each key is one `menu` line (key:<name>:down,key:<name>:up; menuDevQueue steps 30 frames per token) and a 70-frame wait.
# Run (from sunshine-pc): python tools/route.py Strict tools/routes/99_key_matrix.dev --name km_a
#   SUNSHINE_DEV_START=dolpic/0 SUNSHINE_DEV_SKIP_MOVIES=1 SUNSHINE_DEV_SEED=1 SUNSHINE_DEV_PAD_TRACE=1
# Evidence: `[padtrace] read=N buttons=0x.. stick=x,y sub=x,y trig=L,R err=E` lines in run.log (one per change of port 0's
# PADStatus). Attribute them by the `[devscript] wait start line=<L+1>` lines: menu line L is the key, its wait starts the slot.
# Names: Left_Shift and Left_Ctrl stand for SDL's "Left Shift" / "Left Ctrl" (a token has no spaces, launcher.cpp pushKeyToken).
waitfor director mario dirstate=4 camDemo=0 timeout=3000
wait frames=60
log
menu key:Space:down,key:Space:up
wait frames=70
menu key:E:down,key:E:up
wait frames=70
menu key:Q:down,key:Q:up
wait frames=70
menu key:F:down,key:F:up
wait frames=70
menu key:Z:down,key:Z:up
wait frames=70
menu key:Left_Shift:down,key:Left_Shift:up
wait frames=70
menu key:Left_Ctrl:down,key:Left_Ctrl:up
wait frames=70
